ef 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547873 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547873 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547873 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3de2b104-d32f-5800-a490-24878cd6ff1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547951 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d572b8ad-f569-5f9c-bd00-4b949d1c4e59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1938b4fe-a4da-5df4-945e-a4ba43cb2798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547981 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve the equation $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2,$ we raise both sides to the power of $2.$  This allows us to get rid of the radical, and gives us a quadratic equation that is easier to solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3x-8} & =x+2 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{-3x-8})}^{2} & =(x+2)^{2} \\\\ -3x-8 & ={x}^{2}+4x+4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+7x+12 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+(3x+12) & =0 \\\\ x(x+4)+3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember that in square root equations, we should always check the obtained value(s) to ensure that they are actually solutions of the original equation.\n\n- First, we check whether the obtained value $x=-4$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3(-4)-8} & \\overset{?}{=}-4+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{4} & \\overset{?}{=}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\ne -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=-4$ does *not* satisfy the original equation, so we discard it.\n\n- Second, we check whether the obtained value $x=-3$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3(-3)-8} & \\overset{?}{=}-3+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{1} & \\overset{?}{=}-1 \\\\ 1 & \\ne -1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=-3$ does *not* satisfy the original equation, so we discard it.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e49f42fb-4ed5-5c34-8e9e-f41f753d3cfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548068 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve the equation $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1,$ we raise both sides to the power of $2.$  This allows us to get rid of the radical, and gives us a quadratic equation that is easier to solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5x-9} & =x-1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{5x-9})}^{2} & =(x-1)^{2} \\\\ 5x-9 & ={x}^{2}-2x+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(-5x+10) & =0 \\\\ x(x-2)-5(x-2) & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =2,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember that in square root equations, we should always check the obtained value(s) to ensure that they are actually solutions of the original equation.\n\n- First, we check whether the obtained value $x=2$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5(2)-9} & \\overset{?}{=}2-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{1} & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIndeed, the value $x=2$ does satisfy the original equation.\n\n- Second, we check whether the obtained value $x=5$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5(5)-9} & \\overset{?}{=}5-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{16} & \\overset{?}{=}4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIndeed, the value $x=5$ does satisfy the original equation.\n\nTherefore, the solutions of $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1$  are $x=2,\\,5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548098 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548098 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "493c7f13-e45f-5f7f-bf76-16d264e435c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548098 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186547981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548121 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548121 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "701496b1-5d28-5293-9b1c-d814d6e67a7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548121 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186548068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548135 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99997799-e2eb-5bf3-a5f0-77dab9e1f445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548135 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055252 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
